course: dictionary
lesson: 15245
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Shifting can mean moving or changing position, as in «The shifting sand dunes moved again after the storm.» It can also mean changing, as in «Her shifting opinions confused her friends.»
explain: To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Sand dunes are things that move, and an opinion is something you think, so that can change. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Some meanings are only used in certain places or chats. «Shifting furniture took us all afternoon» means moving heavy things, which is hard work. That is an informal use, mostly in the UK, so a dictionary is a good friend when you are not sure.
fact: Shifting is the -ing form of the verb shift.
fact: «Shifting» can mean moving or changing position, like «shifting sand dunes».
fact: «Shifting» can mean changing, like «shifting opinions».
fact: In the UK, informally, «shifting furniture» means moving heavy things, often hard work.
fact: «Shifting gear» means changing gear in a car.
exercise: «The shifting sand dunes moved again after the storm.» What does shifting mean here? | Sleeping quietly | Growing taller | *Moving or changing position | Shining brightly
exercise: Mia says, «Shifting furniture took us all afternoon.» What does shifting mean? | Playing a game with friends | Painting a wall in bright colours | *Moving heavy things, often hard work
exercise: «Her shifting opinions confused her friends.» What does shifting suggest? | Fast asleep | *Changing again and again | Covered in mud | Very tall
test: Dad says, «Shifting gear helped the car climb the hill.» What does shifting gear mean? | Making a cake | Cleaning the windows | Writing a letter | *Changing gear in a car
test: «The shifting shadows made the old barn look spooky.» What does shifting suggest? | Shadows that are very dark and still | *Shadows that keep moving or changing | Shadows made of paper | Shadows shaped like animals
exam: Ella says, «The shifting sands of the desert change every week.» Which meaning fits best? | *Moving or changing position | Shouting loudly | Sad and quiet | Eating slowly
